Unko sharam aani chahiye if they received any iPhones or expensive gifts from anyone this #Diwali. It was reported that several editors of big corporate media houses received #iPhoneDuos as #Diwali gifts, allegedly worth Rs 3 lakh each, from a state/UT Chief Minister who reportedly spent #taxpayers' money to purchase these lavish gifts for news editors.

I strongly believe that big media house editors should not have accepted these #iPhones as gifts, particularly when the government is already spending #crores of rupees on taxpayers' money on advertisements in big corporate media houses.

Indian taxpayers contribute their hard-earned money to the government treasury after working day and night, even in extremely #cold winter conditions, heavy monsoon #rains, and scorching summer #heat. Therefore, public money must be spent responsibly and in the public interest.

In the meantime, I would also like to mention that when I approached advertisers for advertisements for the National Political Mirror, they offered various #excuses. However, despite the financial difficulties that the National Political Mirror and I continue to face in meeting our daily expenses, we remain committed to creativity in #PoliticalJournalism.

I already mentioned my third-best creative concept in the world in my last tweet, which I posted at 1:26 p.m. on November 9. Now, I am sharing my second creative concept in the field of political journalism, reflecting my commitment to #honest journalism and the promotion of young #politicians.

In 2024, as part of this creative initiative, I introduced a new concept in political journalism by presenting a novel idea to recognise gifted and diligent politicians under the headline "2024: #PoliticianOfTheYear."

To continue promoting honest journalism and encouraging young politicians, I reproduced the same concept in 2025 under the heading "2025: Politician of the Year."

In 2025, under my guidance as the founder and editor of the National Political Mirror, the world's only weekly political magazine and India's sole independent media house, I launched a new concept similar to the one I had introduced in 2024.

The final cover page uploaded with this tweet belongs to the 2025 edition of the #NationalPoliticalMirror and is part of a special edition. As its founder and editor, I am proud to announce that the #NationalPoliticalMirror has recognised #NitinNabin as India's most fortunate politician of 2025, awarding him the title of "2025: Politician of the Year."

Additionally, #NationalPoliticalMirror, the #world's only #weekly #political magazine and India's sole #independent media house, awarded him the title of "2025: Politician of the Year" because of his loyalty to the BJP and loyalty to its top leaders and other things about him you can read in the story, which allowed him to be appointed as the new working president of the largest political party in the world in December 2025—a position that is unattainable in any other Indian political party.

For the few people who have doubts about me, I will simply tell you that I know my worth and their worth, including everything.

And believe me, it will take today's big corporate media owners 3,000 years to match my political skills, creativity, and talent, as well as my honesty, credibility, and strong character. I love only one girl, and her name is my late lady of the heart, Ms. #DeepshikhaSinghRana. I also respect all #women because they create the #world, and they are like #gods to me.

And I don't write paid stories, I don't do anything for social media fame, and I don't write any personal remarks about any politicians that would hurt them or their families. Instead, I only write to (related needy people) about lawmakers or politicians who use the money of Indian taxpayers, so I don't fear speaking the truth because I have nothing to lose.

And I strongly believe in personal credibility because if someone has a strong character and personal credibility, it enhances the credibility of their organisation as well.

So I have a strong character and personal credibility, which is why people trust #NationalPoliticalMirror, the #world's only #weekly #political magazine and #India's sole #independent media house.

Lastly, and after getting a journalism degree from one of the world's top journalism schools – the Indian Institute of Mass Communication, a deemed-to-be-university, established on 17 August 1965, in Delhi – I founded #NationalPoliticalMirror to assist those in need and promote honest politics and politicians.

